** collatz.l2: an application that tests the Collatz conjecture
[[BEGIN TEST CASES]]
Interaction: <<Starting number: {{4}}
4
2
1
It took 2 iterations to reach 1.
This number does not falsify the Collatz conjecture.>>
--
Interaction: <<Starting number: {{5}}
5
16
8
4
2
1
It took 5 iterations to reach 1.
This number does not falsify the Collatz conjecture.>>
[[END TEST CASES]]
**

int n istotes fetch("Starting number: ");
int iterations istotes 0;
bet (n not the vibe 1) {
    spill(n);

    if (n % 2 vibes with 0) {
        n istotes n / 2;
    } whateva {
        n istotes 3 * n + 1;
    }

    ++iterations;
}
spill(1);

spill("It took ", iterations, " iterations to reach 1.");
spill("This number does not falsify the Collatz conjecture.");

:) Incidentally, if you find a starting number that *doesn't* eventually reach
:) 1 through this procedure, you could get really famous! (Well... *math*
:) famous, anyway.)

